WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:07.750
Varys: During the great Targaryen civil war
known as "the Dance of the Dragons," a king

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:13.950
and queen each vied for the throne, dividing
their house and its dragons against each other.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:19.020
Eventually, the queen was fed to her rival's
dragon while her son watched, and the victorious

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.000
king soon died of his own wounds.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.890
By the war's end, King's Landing was smashed,
cities razed and sacked never to be rebuilt,

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:30.490
and dragons had faded from this world.

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:35.160
Bronn: There was one Kingsguard (I forgot
the bastard's name) who swore an oath to his

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.840
dying Targaryen king to crown his daughter
after him.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.600
The very night that king died, this Kingsguard
crowned the king's son instead.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.989
When an old man on the Small Council dared
to protest, this honorable knight opened his

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:48.989
throat.

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:53.770
The bastard died in the very civil war he
started along with the old king's son, daughter,

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:55.250
and most of their dragons.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.190
And the Kingsguard?

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:02.820
All that duty and honor and not enough brains
to figure out which Targaryen to give it to.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:07.470
Twin brothers even ended up on opposite sides,
died with tears on their cheeks as they cut

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:08.500
each other down.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:13.830
I suppose I should think that's tragic, but
stupid men do stupid things every day and

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.170
nobody cries over them.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:19.320
Petyr Baelish: As little more than a boy,
Ser Criston Cole replaced the legendary Ser

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.470
Ryam Redwyne on the Kingsguard and soon rose
to Lord Commander.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:26.820
But knights only know one way to settle disputes.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:31.130
When Prince Aegon's father died, Ser Criston
slit the throat of an advisor who objected

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:34.549
to Aegon's ascension over his aunt, the anointed
heir.

00:01:34.549 --> 00:01:39.341
His actions so pleased the new King, Aegon,
Second of His Name, that he appointed Ser

00:01:39.341 --> 00:01:44.470
Criston as his Hand in the ensuing civil war
called the Dance of Dragons.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:49.649
Neither Ser Criston nor the King nor even
the Targaryen dragons would survive it.

00:01:49.649 --> 00:01:54.490
Joffrey Baratheon: Only fear keeps men in
line.

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:56.649
Fear and punishment.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:02:03.640
Then again, torture chambers are just so private.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:08.990
Better to punish your enemies where everyone
can see and remember.

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:14.730
Like that Targaryen who forced his nephew
to watch as he fed the boy's traitor mother

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:16.080
to a dragon.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:20.319
Oh, what I could do with a dragon.

00:02:20.319 --> 00:02:24.750
Euron Greyjoy: Men called him the Red Kraken.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:30.780
During the Dance of Dragons, the Red Kraken
picked the side that was fighting the Lannisters

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:35.000
and fell upon the Westerlands while the Lannisters
were off at war.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:41.390
Casterly Rock itself proved too strong once
the lady of the castle barred its gates, but

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:47.730
the ironborn burned the Lannister fleet and
sacked Lannisport carrying off gold, grain,

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:52.900
and hundreds of women and girls, including
Lord Lannister's favorite mistress and all

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.790
his bastards.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:03:00.940
The Red Kraken now ruled the Sunset Sea as
his forbears had, and his longships again

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:03.680
brought the Old Way to the coast of Westeros.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:09.050
But then the war ended, and the mainland armies
came home.

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:15.400
The Iron Throne commanded the Red Kraken to
stop reaving, and when he didn't, a mistress

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.410
opened his throat as he slept.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:24.680
While his sons squabbled, the Lannisters sent
their soldiers to the Iron Islands.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:30.040
Thousands of men, women, and children were
put to the sword, and scores of villages and

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:33.340
hundreds of longships were put to the torch.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:39.220
The glorious return to the Old Way had lasted
almost two years.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:44.440
Varys: For more than a century, the Targaryens
housed their dragons in the Dragonpit.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:49.440
But dragons are not horses to be stabled or
hounds to be kenneled.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:52.940
With each generation, the dragons became less.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:58.880
Less massive, less swift, less long-lived.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:02.049
Qyburn: And less invulnerable.

00:04:02.049 --> 00:04:07.440
During the Dance of Dragons, two Targaryen
factions killed a handful of their family's

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:08.940
dragons while fighting each other.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:15.810
A frenzied mob even broke into the Dragonpit
and slaughtered the five dragons chained there,

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:22.490
though the last managed to bring down the
roof of the great dome on its assailants.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:26.660
The dragons never recovered their former strength
or numbers.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:34.780
Perhaps their line had been too broken, or
perhaps others intervened to break it further.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:40.340
But the last dragon grew no larger than a
cat, and its death earned Aegon, Third of

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.680
His Name, the epithet "Dragonbane."

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:49.150
Viserys Targaryen: With Dorne in the fold,
and the Faith put in its place, none in Westeros

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:53.710
were left to oppose my family, so we started
opposing each other.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:59.889
In a Dance of Dragons, a Targaryen princess
tried to steal her brother's throne.

00:04:59.889 --> 00:05:05.720
Thanks to her stupidity, most of our dragons
died, though one thankfully ate her before

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:06.720
it did.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:11.240
Shireen Baratheon: "The Dance of Dragons,
A True Telling" by Grand Maester Munkun, being

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:15.801
a history of the war of Targaryen succession
between the Princess Rhaenyra and Aegon, Second

00:05:15.801 --> 00:05:20.310
of His Name, that nearly destroyed the realm.

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:22.289
Viserys Targaryen: "The Dance of the Dragons."

00:05:22.289 --> 00:05:28.770
A stupid name for a Targaryen civil war where
my ancestors danced away my birthright.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:32.220
Before the war, House Targaryen counted eighteen
dragons.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:35.190
By the end, we had two, and nearly as few
Targaryens.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:38.100
We would never be as powerful or as feared
again.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:42.479
The Dance began, as many dances do, with an
old man and a young girl.

00:05:42.479 --> 00:05:46.960
The queen had failed to produce a son for
her king, so he anointed his daughter, the

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:48.540
Princess Rhaenyra, as his heir.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:53.150
But years later, the king remarried, and his
new wife, Queen Alicent of House Hightower,

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:54.240
gave him a son.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:58.530
Feeble and foolish, the old king refused to
change the succession.

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:03.740
He didn't even see how his court had split
into two rival camps of Blacks and Greens,

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:08.080
after the dresses that the princess and the
queen had worn to some tourney.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:15.260
One night, a servant found the old king had
died in his sleep and ran to inform Queen

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:17.110
Alicent.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:21.069
Protocol dictated that the bells would be
rung and a raven sent to Dragonstone to summon

00:06:21.069 --> 00:06:24.400
the heir, Princess Rhaenyra, for her coronation.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.460
But Alicent had other plans.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:31.600
Once she saw her dead husband's body, she
sealed the room and had the servant thrown

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.120
into the Black Cells to ensure his silence.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:39.170
At the hour of the owl, the Lord Commander
of the Kingsguard, Ser Criston Cole, summoned

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:42.020
the small council to inform them of the king's
death.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:46.580
Ser Otto Hightower, the Hand of the King and
father to Queen Alicent, demanded that the

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:49.819
succession be settled immediately.

00:06:49.819 --> 00:06:54.380
The decrepit old men of the small council
were confused; the succession was settled

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:55.490
in their minds.

00:06:55.490 --> 00:07:00.069
The old king had forced the lords of Westeros
to swear fealty to Princess Rhaenyra as his

00:07:00.069 --> 00:07:01.229
heir.

00:07:01.229 --> 00:07:06.940
But SerCriston Cole rightly pointed out that
a son comes before a daughter.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:12.050
The council argued until dawn when the Master
of Coin finally stood up and declared he would

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:13.680
have no part of treason.

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:19.440
SerCriston Cole wisely opened his throat with
a dagger, ending the debate.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:23.380
None were more surprised to hear of Prince
Aegon's succession than Prince Aegon himself.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:28.410
At first, the fool rejected the crown, but
his mother pointed out that his sister Rhaenyra

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:31.770
would return such loyalty by taking his head.

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:35.009
As the old king's trueborn son, he'd always
be a threat.

00:07:35.009 --> 00:07:36.240
Aegon relented.

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:40.550
He was crowned in the Dragonpit, and his wife
and sister Helaena became queen.

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:44.500
His brother Aemondflew off to win over the
few great lords whose support Aegon didn't

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:45.780
already have.

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:50.781
The banner of the gold dragon flew over King's
Landing and the Red Keep as Aegon, Second

00:07:50.781 --> 00:07:53.919
of His Name, ascended the Iron Throne.

00:07:53.919 --> 00:07:56.880
He would not sit it long.

00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:02.050
When ravens carried the news of Aegon's coronation
to Dragonstone, Princess Rhaenyra summoned

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:04.479
her own Black Council.

00:08:04.479 --> 00:08:08.830
With her was her uncle and husband, Daemon
Targaryen, considered by many to be the most

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:11.330
dangerous man in Westeros.

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:15.640
Few lords supported her, but the greatest
of these was CorlysVelaryon, who controlled

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:20.330
the largest fleet in the realm, and his Targaryen
wife Rhaenys, the old king's sister.

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:24.379
Then there were her five sons, although none
grown to manhood.

00:08:24.379 --> 00:08:26.260
A pitiful assembly, really.

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:29.509
Combined they couldn't match the power of
House Hightower alone.

00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:31.970
But Rhaenyra had dragons.

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:39.219
She, Daemon, and Rhaenys rode huge and formidable
beasts, and three of her five sons were riders

00:08:39.219 --> 00:08:40.800
as well.

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:44.830
Dragonstone also housed six more dragons without
riders.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:49.120
Against this, King Aegon had only four dragons
of his own.

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:53.580
Dragons can burn a city, but only armies can
take and hold it.

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:57.670
If she was to prevail, Rhaenyra desperately
needed the support of the few great houses

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:59.670
not already sworn to Aegon.

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:04.550
Her eldest son, Jacaerys, flew to the Vale
and the North, her middle son Lucerys flew

00:09:04.550 --> 00:09:06.020
to the Stormlands.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:12.250
Rhaenyra hoped that the war would begin and,
if the gods were good, end with diplomacy.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:16.640
As always, they weren't.

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:22.610
Robert Baratheon: Little Prince Lucerys must
have wet himself when he entered Storm's End

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:28.200
and found King Aegon's younger brother, Aemond,
already with Lord Baratheon.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:33.440
Aemond was fearsome even before he lost his
eye and set a sapphire in its stead, but the

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:35.890
princeling pleaded his mother's case.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:38.180
Finally, Lord Baratheon made his decision.

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:43.130
"Go home, pup, and tell the bitch, your mother,
that the Lord of Storm's End is not a dog

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:45.160
she can whistle on."

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:49.750
As Aemond's false eyed gleamed at him, the
princeling fled the castle and mounted his

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:51.790
young dragon Arrax.

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:58.760
The rain fell in sheets, and great bolts of
lightning lit the world bright as day.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:04.390
Arrax was struggling to stay aloft in the
gale when a roar shook the very foundations

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:06.700
of Storm's End.

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:12.329
Aemond rose through the clouds and below him
the monstrous Vhagar.

00:10:12.329 --> 00:10:18.590
Vhagar was five times the size of Arrax and
a hardened survivor of a hundred battles.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:21.649
Vhagar caught him above Shipbreaker Bay.

00:10:21.649 --> 00:10:28.579
Watchers on the castle walls saw distant blasts
of flame and heard a shriek drown out the

00:10:28.579 --> 00:10:29.579
thunder.

00:10:29.579 --> 00:10:33.200
Prince Lucerys fell, broken, to be swallowed
by the waves.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:42.190
With his death, the war of ravens came to
an end, and the war of fire and blood began.

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:49.180
Catelyn Stark: When Rhaenyra heard of her
son's death, she collapsed.

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:55.470
She considered ending the war right then until
a raven arrived from her husband, Daemon.

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:59.190
Her son would be avenged.

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:03.300
Whispers slithered through the taverns and
back alleys of Flea Bottom.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:10.269
Two men were found; one was a former gold
cloak, the other a rat catcher in the Red

00:11:10.269 --> 00:11:13.420
Keep who knew all its secrets.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:18.070
History remembers them only as Blood and Cheese.

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:22.470
One night, Queen Helaena entered the royal
apartments with her daughter and two sons

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:24.360
to put them to bed.

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:28.650
Without warning, Blood and Cheese burst in,
daggers in hand.

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:31.230
They told her that a debt was owed.

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:33.310
A son for a son.

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:38.100
Blood and Cheese demanded she choose which
son would be ripped from her forever.

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:43.220
Queen Helaena pleaded with the men to kill
her instead, but they refused.

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:47.970
Weeping, Helaena named her younger son Maelor.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:53.370
Perhaps she thought the boy was too young
to understand, perhaps because the older boy

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:56.920
was King Aegon's firstborn son and heir.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:59.709
"You hear that, little boy?"

00:11:59.709 --> 00:12:02.060
Cheese whispered to the younger son.

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:05.510
"Your mama wants you dead."

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:09.700
Then Blood struck off the older boy's head
with a single blow.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:14.850
When the guards burst in, they found Queen
Helaena still screaming, clasping her dead

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:18.490
son's body to her, mad with grief.

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:23.029
The blood of her children transformed a dynastic
dispute into a war of annihilation.

00:12:23.029 --> 00:12:29.800
The grief and rage of losing a child could
burn down the world.

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:35.800
Either Aegon or Rhaenyra could live at the
end, but not both.

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:40.120
Viserys: Rhaenyra's forces struck yet another
blow.

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:44.579
The moment the Lord of Harrenhal saw Daemon
Targaryen circling the castle on his dragon

00:12:44.579 --> 00:12:47.990
Caraxes, he struck his banners and surrendered.

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:52.140
The Blacks now had the strongest castle in
the Riverlands.

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:56.880
Darker news still came to Aegon; thanks to
Rhaenyra's sons, Winterfell had declared for

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.290
Rhaenyra, as had the Vale.

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:04.029
Furious, Aegon dismissed his grandfather,
Ser Otto, as Hand and appointed SerCriston

00:13:04.029 --> 00:13:08.510
Cole, who swore to march on all the lords
who had declared for Rhaenyra and put their

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:09.810
castles to the torch.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:15.760
Cole and the royal army first marched north
and laid siege to Rook's Rest, a Black stronghold

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:16.980
near Dragonstone.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:21.480
When the Lord saw their approach, he sent
a raven to Rhaenyra begging for help.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:26.899
For days he watched his fields and villages
burning, with no response from his queen.

00:13:26.899 --> 00:13:30.899
Until one day, a shadow passed over the Green
army.

00:13:30.899 --> 00:13:36.360
Rhaenyra had sent not an army, but her former
mother-by-law Rhaenys and her dragon Meleys.

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:42.399
As her ancestor had done at the Field of Fire,
Rhaenys gleefully began to incinerate SerCriston's

00:13:42.399 --> 00:13:43.399
army.

00:13:43.399 --> 00:13:47.630
But Aegon had set a trap, and Rhaenys had
flown right into it.

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:53.370
As Rhaenys and Meleys blanketed SerCriston's
troops in dragonflame, two other dragons rose

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:55.149
into the sky.

00:13:55.149 --> 00:13:59.050
Aemond on Vhagar and King Aegon himself on
the gleaming Sunfyre.

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:02.600
To her credit, Rhaenys didn't flee.

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:07.870
Dragon fought dragons, and a second sun blossomed
in the sky.

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:12.269
When the smoke cleared, only Aemond and Vhagar
stood uninjured.

00:14:12.269 --> 00:14:16.910
Sunfyre, the most magnificent dragon in the
world, had one of its wings almost completely

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:18.970
torn from its body.

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:23.889
Trapped beneath Sunfyre was the king himself,
broken and burned so badly in places that

00:14:23.889 --> 00:14:27.000
his armor had fused onto his flesh.

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:31.680
His body survived, but his mind was given
over to milk of the poppy.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:38.680
Meleys had been torn to shreds, and her rider,
Rhaenys, was a pile of ash.

00:14:38.680 --> 00:14:43.120
Panicked by the defeat, Rhaenyra shipped her
two youngest sons across the Narrow Sea for

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:44.120
their protection.

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:49.350
Only for her youngest to return days later,
clinging to the neck of his wounded and dying

00:14:49.350 --> 00:14:50.350
dragon.

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:54.519
He and his brother had been set upon by an
enemy fleet just off Dragonstone.

00:14:54.519 --> 00:14:59.639
Defying his mother's command, Rhaenyra's eldest
son and heir, Jacaerys, mounted his dragon

00:14:59.639 --> 00:15:03.240
Vermaxand flew to rescue his other brother
and punish the enemy fleet.

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:09.779
But the foolish boy let Vermax be hooked like
a trout and dragged into the sea, where he

00:15:09.779 --> 00:15:12.570
soaked up even more arrows than seawater.

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:17.130
His brother disappeared over the horizon or
beneath the waves.

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:18.570
No one could say for sure.

00:15:18.570 --> 00:15:23.210
With the loss of four dragons, Rhaenyra's
only advantage was fading.

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:28.970
Luckily for her, over the centuries, House
Targaryen had spilled more than blood on Dragonstone.

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:33.579
She promised gold and title to any of the
Targaryen bastards who could tame the six

00:15:33.579 --> 00:15:35.950
untamed dragons on the island.

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:41.209
These bastards were called the dragonseeds,
though most were called supper.

00:15:41.209 --> 00:15:46.100
Perhaps the dragons were eventually sated
or bored, but four of them accepted riders

00:15:46.100 --> 00:15:48.870
and were enlisted in Rhaenyra's cause.

00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:53.759
Robert: After Rook's Rest, Aemond One-Eye
took command of the Greens from his crippled

00:15:53.759 --> 00:15:55.959
and poppy-addled brother.

00:15:55.959 --> 00:16:00.839
Aemond was the blood of the dragon, and dragons
don't cower behind city walls.

00:16:00.839 --> 00:16:06.550
He marched the king's army north to take back
Harrenhal from Rhaenyra's husband, Daemon.

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:12.509
But when he and Criston Cole reached the castle,
they found the gates open, with Daemon and

00:16:12.509 --> 00:16:14.760
all his men gone.

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:20.860
That night they feasted their victory; Daemon
had fled rather than face their wrath.

00:16:20.860 --> 00:16:24.540
But Daemon was more snake than dragon.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:30.870
As Aemond marched north, he'd flown Caraxes
south, slithering past the Green army over

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:33.320
the waters of the Gods Eye.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:38.680
One day King's Landing looked up and saw two
dragons circling their foul city.

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:45.000
Daemon and Rhaenyra had come for her throne,
for the city was defenseless.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:51.750
Aemond had taken the king's army from the
city, and worse, he'd taken his dragon Vhagar.

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:57.300
Seeing that resistance was hopeless, the small
council surrendered the city, the Queen Mother

00:16:57.300 --> 00:17:00.360
Alicent, and the broken Queen Helaena.

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:03.100
But not King Aegon.

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:09.160
Somehow, despite his wounds and delirium,
he had vanished from the city.

00:17:09.160 --> 00:17:15.449
And so Queen Rhaenyra climbed the steps and
seated herself of the Iron Throne.

00:17:15.449 --> 00:17:21.020
Legend has it that as she left that hall later,
blood trickled down her legs and hands, proving

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:24.490
the Iron Throne had spurned her.

00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:25.579
Nonsense!

00:17:25.579 --> 00:17:28.419
It's a chair made of steel blades.

00:17:28.419 --> 00:17:33.730
Rhaenyra had wanted it all her life and had
sacrificed two sons for it.

00:17:33.730 --> 00:17:37.450
She likely gripped the damn thing too tight.

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:43.380
Viserys: When Aemond realized that his arrogance
had cost him the capital, he mounted Vhagar

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:49.590
in a black rage and rained fire onto every
village and castle he suspected of disloyalty.

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:53.910
Abandoned by Aemond, SerCriston marched the
royal army back to King's Landing, intent

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:55.919
on recapturing the city himself.

00:17:55.919 --> 00:18:00.580
Instead, he was trapped and cut to pieces
by the Riverlords, who had sworn to support

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:01.580
Rhaenyra's claim.

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:06.789
When a new army of Green loyalists marched
up from the Reach and laid siege to the city

00:18:06.789 --> 00:18:11.530
of Tumbleton, Rhaenyra sent two of her dragonseeds
to lay waste to them.

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:15.820
Instead, the dragonseeds proved their bastard
nature and betrayed her.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:19.809
They burned the city and all the Black forces
garrisoned within.

00:18:19.809 --> 00:18:24.850
Lucky for her, they didn't turn towards King's
Landing but whored and drank in the ruins

00:18:24.850 --> 00:18:29.630
with the Greens, who were victorious and somewhat
confused.

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:35.120
Oberyn Martell: Rhaenyra now mistrusted all
the dragonseeds, including the girl who rode

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:39.750
with her husband Daemon, hunting Aemond in
the Riverlands.

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:42.580
She ordered the girl's head be sent to her.

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:47.070
But there was a complication.

00:18:47.070 --> 00:18:51.450
As well as her dragon, the girl had taken
to riding Daemon.

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:55.730
When Daemon received the queen's order, he
proclaimed it a queen's words and a whore's

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:56.730
work.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:19:02.010
He sent the girl away at dawn, watching her
and her dragon vanish into the morning mists.

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:10.120
Then Daemon sent a challenge to his nephew
Aemond and flew to Harrenhal alone to wait.

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:15.490
Fourteen days later, a shadow blacker than
any passing cloud swept over Harrenhal.

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:21.610
Vhagar had come at last and on her rode one-eyed
Prince Aemond.

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:23.590
He mocked Daemon for facing him alone.

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:25.900
"You have lived too long, uncle."

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:30.210
And Daemon replied, "On that much, we agree."

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:35.380
Then the old prince climbed stiffly onto the
back of his dragon Caraxes but neglected to

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:38.870
fasten the chains that secured rider to saddle.

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:44.570
The sun was close to setting when, as one,
the two dragons leaped into the sky.

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:48.480
Daemon took Caraxes up swiftly until he disappeared
into a bank of clouds.

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:51.690
Vhagar, older and slower, ascended more gradually.

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:56.309
Up and up, Vhagar soared, searching for Caraxes.

00:19:56.309 --> 00:20:00.429
Sudden as a thunderbolt, a shrieking Caraxes
dove upon Vhagar.

00:20:00.429 --> 00:20:03.299
Locked together, the dragons tumbled toward
the lake.

00:20:03.299 --> 00:20:08.121
Caraxes' jaws closed upon Vhagar's neck, but
Vhagar ripped open Caraxes's belly, and her

00:20:08.121 --> 00:20:10.210
teeth ripped off a wing.

00:20:10.210 --> 00:20:13.190
The lake rushed up with terrible speed.

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:19.210
Then Daemon Targaryen, who had never fastened
his riding chains, stood in his saddle.

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:24.760
He leaped from his dragon to Aemond's, and
in his hand was Dark Sister, the Valyrian

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:27.960
sword of Aegon's sister-queen Visenya.

00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:33.080
As Aemond One-Eye looked up in terror, Daemon
ripped off his nephew's helm and drove the

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:39.140
sword down into his one remaining eye so hard
the point came out the back of the young prince's

00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:40.140
throat.

00:20:40.140 --> 00:20:45.950
Half a heartbeat later, the dragons struck
the lake, sending up a gout of water so high

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:50.760
that it was said to have been as tall as Harrenhal's
great tower.

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:56.820
The lake boiled with dragon blood and then
was still.

00:20:56.820 --> 00:21:00.490
Daemon Targaryen was nine-and-forty at his
death.

00:21:00.490 --> 00:21:03.309
Prince Aemond had only turned twenty.

00:21:03.309 --> 00:21:11.630
Vhagar, the greatest of the Targaryen dragons,
had counted one-hundred-and-eighty-one years.

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:16.090
Thus passed the last living creature from
the days of Aegon's Conquest.

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:22.680
Viserys: Back in King's Landing, Queen Rhaenyra
didn't have much time to grieve for her stupid

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:23.680
husband.

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:27.770
The mad former queen Helaena flung herself
from a balcony, to be impaled upon the iron

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:30.750
spikes lining the moat of Maegor's Holdfast.

00:21:30.750 --> 00:21:36.420
That night, the city rose in riot against
Rhaenyra, demanding justice for Queen Helaena

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:41.090
and her murdered son, among other foolish
peasantfantasies.

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:46.360
In the midst of this chaos, a one-handed fool
called the Shepherd began to rant against

00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:47.360
dragons.

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:50.160
Not just the ones of the enemy, but all dragons
everywhere.

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:56.419
As he pointed to the Dragonpit above on the
hill, he shouted, "There the demons dwell,

00:21:56.419 --> 00:21:57.419
this is their city.

00:21:57.419 --> 00:22:00.919
If you would make it yours, first you must
destroy them."

00:22:00.919 --> 00:22:05.700
A cry went up from ten thousand throats, "Kill
them!"

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:09.330
There were four dragons housed within the
Dragonpit that night.

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:15.880
By the time the first of the attackers came
pouring in, all four were roused, awake and

00:22:15.880 --> 00:22:16.880
angry.

00:22:16.880 --> 00:22:19.290
Nobody knows how many men and women died that
night.

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:20.290
Who cares?

00:22:20.290 --> 00:22:21.960
They all should have!

00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:25.080
Trapped within the pit, the dragons could
not fly.

00:22:25.080 --> 00:22:28.680
Instead, they fought with horns, claws, teeth,
and fire.

00:22:28.680 --> 00:22:34.330
For every man who died, ten more appeared,
shouting that the dragons must die.

00:22:34.330 --> 00:22:36.980
One by one, they did.

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:41.320
Finally, the last remaining dragon broke her
chain, spread her wings, and flew straight

00:22:41.320 --> 00:22:43.870
up at the great dome trying to flee.

00:22:43.870 --> 00:22:48.690
Already weakened by dragonflame, the dome
cracked under the force of impact and then

00:22:48.690 --> 00:22:53.309
tumbled down, crushing the dragonslayers and
herself.

00:22:53.309 --> 00:22:58.600
Joffrey Baratheon: High atop the Red Keep,
Queen Rhaenyra clutched her two remaining

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:04.650
sons to her as she watched the end of her
family's might, too afraid of the peasants

00:23:04.650 --> 00:23:06.559
to defend her dragons.

00:23:06.559 --> 00:23:10.669
At least her older son, Joffrey, had a man's
spine.

00:23:10.669 --> 00:23:15.740
He stole his mother's dragon Syrax and tried
to fly it to the Dragonpit to save his birthright.

00:23:15.740 --> 00:23:22.230
But the stupid beast didn't understand and
twisted beneath him, fighting to be free of

00:23:22.230 --> 00:23:26.480
the little boy, until it was.

00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:32.480
A queen is still a woman, with all the weakness
of that sex.

00:23:32.480 --> 00:23:38.350
Weeping for her lost son more than her dragons,
Rhaenyra abandoned the Iron Throne and sold

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:43.610
her crown to buy passage for her and her last
son back to Dragonstone.

00:23:43.610 --> 00:23:47.500
Rhaenyra hoped to hatch more dragons from
the eggs in the castle.

00:23:47.500 --> 00:23:53.520
But when she landed, the welcoming party slew
her guards and marched her and her son at

00:23:53.520 --> 00:23:59.570
spearpoint to the castle to face a dead man
and a dying dragon.

00:23:59.570 --> 00:24:00.720
"Sister!"

00:24:00.720 --> 00:24:04.059
King Aegon, Second of His Name, called out
to Rhaenyra.

00:24:04.059 --> 00:24:11.070
Rook's Rest had left Aegon bent and twisted,
his once handsome face puffy from the milk

00:24:11.070 --> 00:24:15.520
of the poppy, with burn scars covering half
his body.

00:24:15.520 --> 00:24:20.909
Rhaenyra, ever defiant, told her dear brother
that she'd hoped he was dead.

00:24:20.909 --> 00:24:22.850
"After you!"

00:24:22.850 --> 00:24:24.600
Aegon answered.

00:24:24.600 --> 00:24:35.570
Then Sunfyre bathed her in a blast of flame
and devoured her in six bites while her son

00:24:35.570 --> 00:24:43.470
watched, leaving the seventh and final bite,
her lower leg, for the Stranger.

00:24:43.470 --> 00:24:49.840
Viserys: Rhaenyra was dead, and King Aegon
sat the Iron Throne again.

00:24:49.840 --> 00:24:52.480
But only for half a year.

00:24:52.480 --> 00:24:56.830
He was poisoned by his own men and replaced
with the very boy who had watched his mother

00:24:56.830 --> 00:24:58.220
devoured.

00:24:58.220 --> 00:25:04.950
Shireen: When Rhaenyra's last son wed Aegon's
only daughter, the Dance of Dragons officially

00:25:04.950 --> 00:25:05.950
ended.

00:25:05.950 --> 00:25:08.279
Ash and burned men.

00:25:08.279 --> 00:25:10.840
All that was left of the Riverlands.

00:25:10.840 --> 00:25:14.870
Two scared children spouting oaths they didn't
understand.

00:25:14.870 --> 00:25:18.830
All that was left of the mighty House Targaryen.

00:25:18.830 --> 00:25:23.660
Ancient skulls and hatchlings that grew no
bigger than cats.

00:25:23.660 --> 00:25:31.929
All that was left of the dragons.

